Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||11-28-2000||02:55 PM||||for a while know my car has ben hard to start.  you would turn the ignition swith as far as it would go and nothing.  then I would slowly back off till I would hear the starter click then stop there and it would go ahead and start up just fine.  But as of yesterday, it has become damn near imposiible to get it to click over.  I have to take they key in and out and wiggle it  around and if I get lucky it will hit that certian little area that will let it click over.  So I guess my questions are 10 is this the igniton switch? 2) if not what else could it be? 3)how much is a new ignition 4) I have taken the steering column apart before and it was hard, so would I be correct in assuming that replacing the switch would not be easy?<P>well any help in the matter would be greatly appreciated!  <BR>ps- is the ignition switch fiero specific, or is it one of thoose things gm used on every car in 86?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||11-28-2000||03:29 PM||||The "keyed" switch is just a machanical device. It has a female slot in the end that goes into the column and it slips over a male key inside. When you insert your ignition key, all it does is allow you to twist that male key. The male key then pulls a metal rod that operates the electrical switch mounted to the base of your steering column. <P>My guess is the electrical switch has either gone bad or is loose and out of adjustment. Look at the base of the column and see if you can physically move the switch. If you can, you can adjust it to the proper position the ecure it with the two mounting bolts (if they havent fallen out and been vacuumed up).<P>If the switch seems secure and your sure the metal rod is moving with the "keyed" switch, then most likly the electrical switch has gone bad.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||11-28-2000||04:00 PM||||More than likely it's the ignition switch module.  It sits on the steering column down from the key slot.  The steering wheel is easy to lower and you can do the whole job in less than an hour.  The are two points where the column is held in place.  One is up towards the steering wheel .  First remove the plastic cover under the steering wheel and dash.  You will see 4 brass looking bolts on a plate.  This plate is held in place by a bolt on either side which can be seen by looking straight up on either side of the column.  Take them off and the 4 bolts.  Further down towards the floor is another rounder looking collar held in place also by two bolts.  After you take them out the column will lower down if it hasn't already fallen on you by then.  You'll see the module which has a rod running into it from the key lock assmbly.  Change that module and you should be smiling.  Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dan86gt3.8||11-28-2000||04:25 PM||||thansk for the info guys!  what is this switch called and can you get it at autozone?<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-28-2000||07:48 PM||||It's called an ignition switch....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>A more exact discription of the setup it this.<P>The key lock slides into a gear on the end. The lock gear moves a rack gear that is connected to a linkage that runs down the column. to the switch.<P>If you know how the rack and pinion steering works this is pretty much the same idea.<P>First thing to do is drop the column and see if the switch has come loose. that happens quite regularly with GM.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
